# LLM Adapter System — Multi-Provider Architecture Plan

## Overview & Goal

Currently, the backend directly imports and uses Google's `genai` SDK (`gemini_client`) across generators, RAG embedders, chat routers, and the LangGraph Web Research Agent.

To enable switching to **Local LLMs (Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM)**, **DeepSeek**, **Anthropic Claude**, or **OpenAI** without changing any business logic, we will build a **Unified LLM Adapter Layer** (`backend/core/llm/`).

---

## Target Architecture

```
                               ┌───────────────────────────┐
                               │ Business Logic / Services │
                               │ (generators, RAG, agent)  │
                               └─────────────┬─────────────┘
                                             │
                                             ▼
                             ┌──────────────────────────────┐
                             │    Unified LLM Adapter API   │
                             │   (llm.generate / llm.embed) │
                             └───────────────┬──────────────┘
                                             │
      ┌──────────────────────┬───────────────┼───────────────┬──────────────────────┐
      ▼                      ▼               ▼               ▼                      ▼
┌───────────┐        ┌───────────────┐ ┌───────────┐ ┌───────────────┐      ┌─────────────┐
│  Gemini   │        │ OpenRouter /  │ │ DeepSeek  │ │   Ollama /    │      │  Anthropic  │
│ Provider  │        │ OpenAI Format │ │ Provider  │ │ Local Models  │      │  Provider   │
└───────────┘        └───────────────┘ └───────────┘ └───────────────┘      └─────────────┘
```

---

## Key Components to Build

### 1. Unified Interface (`backend/core/llm/base.py`)
Abstract base class defining standardized methods:
- `generate(prompt, system_prompt, temperature, json_mode) -> str`
- `embed(texts: List[str]) -> List[List[float]]`

### 2. Concrete Provider Implementations (`backend/core/llm/providers/`)
- `GeminiProvider`: Uses `google-genai` (default)
- `OpenAICompatibleProvider`: Works for **DeepSeek**, **Ollama (local)**, **vLLM**, **LM Studio**, **OpenAI**, **Groq**, **Together AI**
- `AnthropicProvider`: Supports Claude Opus / Sonnet natively or via Anthropic API
- `FastEmbed / HuggingFace Provider`: Local embedding alternative (e.g. `BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5` or `sentence-transformers`) so RAG can run 100% offline with local LLMs.

### 3. Factory & Configuration (`backend/core/llm/factory.py` & `.env.local`)
Dynamic provider instantiation driven by `.env.local` settings:

```bash
# Environment Configuration (.env.local)

# Select active provider: 'gemini' | 'ollama' | 'deepseek' | 'anthropic' | 'openai'
LLM_PROVIDER=gemini
LLM_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
LLM_API_KEY=your_key_here
LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1 # Used for Ollama / local endpoints

# Embedding Configuration
EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=gemini # 'gemini' | 'local' (sentence-transformers/fastembed)
EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-004
```

---

## Proposed Changes & Refactoring

### Core Module (`backend/core/`)

#### [NEW] [base.py](file:///home/sumit/Desktop/Untitled%20Folder%202/backend/core/llm/base.py)
Abstract base provider interface (`BaseLLMProvider` and `BaseEmbeddingProvider`).

#### [NEW] [factory.py](file:///home/sumit/Desktop/Untitled%20Folder%202/backend/core/llm/factory.py)
Global `get_llm()` and `get_embedder()` functions that read `.env.local` and return configured provider instances.

#### [NEW] [providers/](file:///home/sumit/Desktop/Untitled%20Folder%202/backend/core/llm/providers/)
Individual provider files (`gemini.py`, `openai_compat.py`, `anthropic.py`, `local_embed.py`).

#### [MODIFY] [gemini_client.py](file:///home/sumit/Desktop/Untitled%20Folder%202/backend/core/gemini_client.py)
Maintain backward-compatible shim pointing to `get_llm()`.

---

### RAG & Generator Modules

#### [MODIFY] [embedder.py](file:///home/sumit/Desktop/Untitled%20Folder%202/backend/rag/embedder.py)
Replace direct `gemini_client.models.embed_content` calls with `get_embedder().embed(texts)`.

#### [MODIFY] [summary.py](file:///home/sumit/Desktop/Untitled%20Folder%202/backend/generators/summary.py)
Replace direct Gemini call with `get_llm().generate(...)`.

#### [MODIFY] [notes.py](file:///home/sumit/Desktop/Untitled%20Folder%202/backend/generators/notes.py)
Replace direct Gemini call with `get_llm().generate(...)`.

#### [MODIFY] [flashcards.py](file:///home/sumit/Desktop/Untitled%20Folder%202/backend/generators/flashcards.py)
Replace direct Gemini call with `get_llm().generate(..., json_mode=True)`.

#### [MODIFY] [mindmap.py](file:///home/sumit/Desktop/Untitled%20Folder%202/backend/generators/mindmap.py)
Replace direct Gemini call with `get_llm().generate(..., json_mode=True)`.

#### [MODIFY] [chat.py](file:///home/sumit/Desktop/Untitled%20Folder%202/backend/routers/chat.py)
Replace direct Gemini call with `get_llm().generate(...)`.

#### [MODIFY] [nodes.py](file:///home/sumit/Desktop/Untitled%20Folder%202/backend/web_research_agent/nodes.py)
Replace direct Gemini calls across all 5 graph nodes (`plan`, `search` query refinement, `analyze`, `write_report`) with `get_llm().generate(...)`.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **OpenAI API Standard Compatibility:** Most modern providers (DeepSeek, Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM, Groq, Together, Mistral) support OpenAI's standard HTTP API format (`/v1/chat/completions`). Using `httpx` or `openai` Python SDK covers 90% of all alternative LLM providers seamlessly.

> [!TIP]
> **100% Offline Mode:** For running local LLMs (e.g. via Ollama), vector embeddings can be set to `EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=local` using `fastembed` or `sentence-transformers`, making the entire research assistant work offline without any external API keys!

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Verification
1. Test switching `LLM_PROVIDER=gemini` in `.env.local` and running `python3 -c "from core.llm.factory import get_llm; print(get_llm().generate('Hello'))"`.
2. Test switching `LLM_PROVIDER=ollama` / `LLM_PROVIDER=deepseek` with fallback mock or live endpoint.
3. Test embedding generation via `get_embedder().embed(["test"])`.
4. Run full agent & RAG test suite to verify zero regressions.

